#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100642 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dbb4e0a0-55ec-5cc7-9617-99cec8108940" :question/math-academy-id "e-540" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100646 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "891e9004-961b-539a-ab93-0752347fd077" :question/math-academy-id "e-541" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dc3f3e0-ff57-5efd-bd2a-2ae7c331785c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290335} {:answer/id #uuid "13cc58bb-55ce-5b90-bc27-e0d82b697e61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290336} {:answer/id #uuid "c22f6665-5738-56da-b581-b8d90a921abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290337} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf097b4-cf1f-5a26-939d-f3154132a89b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y=-2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290338} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1214e9-480e-5e00-9d58-fabbe34483df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13cc58bb-55ce-5b90-bc27-e0d82b697e61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290336} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb92c282-cf61-5b85-93a2-fb47c1fb258d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2470563-1a2f-5e0a-b7d9-e6883d815fd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104055" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =x+C \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =-x-C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-0-C \\\\ 0 & =0-C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d948bac9-62a7-5665-95df-522f8b717271" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{2x+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292417} {:answer/id #uuid "9a755514-92bb-506a-8775-2d1708304b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292418} {:answer/id #uuid "c027f59a-7575-5547-8e1a-bc2ccbcccf58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{x}{1+x+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292419} {:answer/id #uuid "cf27878b-c87e-50bf-a22a-f8c50efcdbc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292420} {:answer/id #uuid "b5984bc1-4d99-5874-a48a-f57bbe65a914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{2+2x-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf27878b-c87e-50bf-a22a-f8c50efcdbc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292420} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ce8856-c1f6-5ff7-bc9a-c230fc99d9dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "919dc14f-ff69-5952-b9d3-1351ffc6437d" :question/math-academy-id "q-104059" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(-1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+x+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{1-(-1)^{2}-C(-1)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{C} & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312762 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de00ee50-8fcd-56a0-80c9-ce55068425a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+8{x}^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312764} {:answer/id #uuid "8a8a68c0-e78f-5b95-9b4d-daac33153ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8{x}^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312765} {:answer/id #uuid "033fdcc9-58c7-5818-908c-7a1b4029fcf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312766} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c4af94-99f3-5b11-a092-e4831c2dad7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312767} {:answer/id #uuid "8106d8c2-18a0-547d-bee4-ccf27f8da73e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5c4af94-99f3-5b11-a092-e4831c2dad7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312767} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c26e6cf-2d22-5091-8bf9-ee65799df215" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e80102fb-b0d5-5bdb-8b2c-e58b30c1b434" :question/math-academy-id "q-104065" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}.$ Assume that $0<x<\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+4{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the right-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nwhere $C={C}_{1}+{C}_{2}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})+4{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡1+{\\pi }^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3f0397d-f762-54ab-bfdd-1867271964b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-{e}^{-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312771} {:answer/id #uuid "a20b712f-91dc-571d-9d75-f5df1c22a9f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-1+{e}^{-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312772} {:answer/id #uuid "8af44e4c-6c1f-53ac-bc8c-919b300a5c71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-1-{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312773} {:answer/id #uuid "60665b18-fb0e-5871-befd-870df448dc57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-1+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312774} {:answer/id #uuid "5eaa1435-aec7-50ba-bc0b-1db151160857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3f0397d-f762-54ab-bfdd-1867271964b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-{e}^{-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312771} :answer-field/id #uuid "95c9a681-e457-5107-8106-bb2d53d5a093" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a106a954-1ab0-5359-b8c4-675966fee9cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-14312" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{-x}$ that satisfies $y(0)={e}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,dx & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{e}^{-x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-{e}^{-x}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{e}^{-x}+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{-{e}^{-x}+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{-{e}^{-x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)={e}^{-1}$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} & =K{e}^{-{e}^{-0}} \\\\ {e}^{-1} & =K{e}^{-1} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{-x}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)={e}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-{e}^{-x}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16561ff9-49cc-5c8d-9d91-80496b61032b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x^2+2)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290356} {:answer/id #uuid "abaa3130-f455-5f4c-bc41-d1d85b638552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x^2+3)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16561ff9-49cc-5c8d-9d91-80496b61032b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x^2+2)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290356} :answer-field/id #uuid "abcfd3ba-e3c9-5721-a8d2-3b248e6bea2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e61295b6-6138-5875-8867-aee2da069121" :question/math-academy-id "q-355528" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\sqrt{y}$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(1)=9.$  Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & =2{x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2} \\\\ y & ={({x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $y>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+C)^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=9$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =((1)^{2}+C)^{2} \\\\ 9 & =(1+C)^{2} \\\\ 3 & =1+C \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+2)^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfdc97e1-e0ec-505d-8873-6e496bf4b877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x^2/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfdc97e1-e0ec-505d-8873-6e496bf4b877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x^2/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312779} :answer-field/id #uuid "910d6a58-2678-5801-bc3d-52e3e8d75283" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86ea9e27-7410-5a64-bcd2-b11d02609395" :question/math-academy-id "q-355562" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=xy$  that satisfies $y(0)=1.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/2+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/2+C}\\, \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}/2+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =K{e}^{0} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=xy$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{{x}^{2}/2}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78623355-e38a-5ca6-82fc-0ede5c4c9a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78623355-e38a-5ca6-82fc-0ede5c4c9a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290366} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c75e092-6079-5be0-bdeb-81cf428bb1cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed0df24d-07b8-5d65-9f2d-72f21abe2584" :question/math-academy-id "q-355577" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ec52982-94be-5d1f-baef-e86249afe96c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2-1/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312782} {:answer/id #uuid "53a823d4-ace3-5415-83d3-0905a1781274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{1-1/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ec52982-94be-5d1f-baef-e86249afe96c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2-1/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312782} :answer-field/id #uuid "786e4bda-f2b8-5dd2-b35d-3354a644b176" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ccd0d28-c2a6-553d-8006-d97ec4bdd759" :question/math-academy-id "q-355578" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}=0$  that satisfies $y(1)=e.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-1/x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-1/x+C}\\, \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-1/x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{-1/x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=e$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e & =K{e}^{-1} \\\\ K & ={e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=e$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2-1/x}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7a3bc39-a922-5f64-bfd1-2a19006f0aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4x+{e}^{-3x}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296410} {:answer/id #uuid "9873e707-2fd2-5249-a343-87db775dbe1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296411} {:answer/id #uuid "96361bee-48b6-5d73-b545-1b1ca709bc20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x+{e}^{-3x}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296412} {:answer/id #uuid "e083fe15-44ca-5ac8-bc24-f2c898194dce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296413} {:answer/id #uuid "db8ab467-ee18-56ba-90df-79102eaa92a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9873e707-2fd2-5249-a343-87db775dbe1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296411} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a28f488-2cc3-5e9b-baa4-b221f207a20a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b83618f6-c01a-5048-a3a3-6b622350db67" :question/math-academy-id "q-79371" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(0)=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x} & =3 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+2x{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{e}^{-x}+2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{e}^{-x}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-3{e}^{-x}+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=-3$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-3 \\\\ -3{e}^{-0}+{0}^{2}+C & =-3 \\\\ C-3 & =-3 \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-3$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b23911a-877a-5e80-8175-132810929a84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312786} {:answer/id #uuid "5155c528-33b5-51dd-84fa-cafed472a4e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312787} {:answer/id #uuid "fa790788-a417-5e4e-b69f-a99f474a6e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312788} {:answer/id #uuid "c60ed70a-2599-5383-95f7-650d0857f471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{4}-x+2}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312789} {:answer/id #uuid "79d1a842-07f7-57e7-b42c-950fee6afbcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79d1a842-07f7-57e7-b42c-950fee6afbcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312790} :answer-field/id #uuid "271a6a6e-af64-539e-b578-ddb2b11702e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5584487-f86c-5569-83ea-05d79037610f" :question/math-academy-id "q-79373" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(4{x}^{3}-1){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}-1 \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{4}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{4}-1+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡C & =0 \\\\ C & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1).\n$$"}]}
